name easyfig
category Package
revision 64967
shortdesc Simplifying the use of common figures
relocated 1
longdesc The package provides the command \Figure[<key=value>...]{<image
longdesc filename>} to simplify the business of including an image as
longdesc figure in the most common form (centred and with caption and
longdesc label). Caption and label are set using the caption and label
longdesc keys; the label fig:<image filename> is used if none is given.
longdesc If the here key is given, the figure is not 'floated', and the
longdesc user is responsible for placement. The package uses the
longdesc author's package adjustbox to centre an image and to simplify
longdesc further modifications. As adjustbox now provides keys to turn
longdesc images or other material into floats or non-floats, including
longdesc captions, easyfig has become quite redundant.
runfiles size=2
 RELOC/tex/latex/easyfig/easyfig.sty
catalogue-contact-bugs https://github.com/MartinScharrer/easyfig/issues
catalogue-contact-home https://github.com/MartinScharrer/easyfig
catalogue-contact-repository https://github.com/MartinScharrer/easyfig.git
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/easyfig
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics float graphics-use
catalogue-version 1.2a
